S[81] = "5.4 Capital-level measurement consequences"
S[82] = None
S[83] = ("From ⟦TFP=log Y−α log K−(1−α) log LH⟧, any change in measured capital changes measured TFP mechanically. Figure 3 plots ⟦K_{obs}/K_{M0}−1⟧ for six countries. In every country the observable-lag stock lies below the standard PIM stock on average over 2010–2019, and the gap widens as investment shifts towards longer-gestation assets. Under the calibrated lags, this gap measures how far a zero-lag PIM counts investment as productive before gestation is complete. All 35 country means are negative; Greece is positive only in 2014–2019 (+0.7% on average), against a −0.6% mean over the window.")
